The team is great and the boys really like to play. Workouts are going well.
I hope that we can move on, leave the last season behind and be successful.”
Fear about retirement savings keeps women awake
Although the people taking part in the survey knew exactly how they wanted them to be taken care of, few talked about it with their family.
In a study conducted by Nationwide, about half of the participants said they had spoken to their spouse about the cost of long-term care.
Only 10 percent said they talked about it with their children.
“People want them to be dealt with by a family member, but they don’t talk about it,” said Holly Snyder, vice-president at Nationwide, who sells life insurance.
Where do we begin?
Speak to your spouse and children: “You won’t prepare your family to take care of yourself if you don’t express your will beforehand.
Together with an adviser and your family, talk about where and how you want to be looked after, because this choice will be an important factor in determining costs.
Ask a financial adviser for help: It can help you find a way to pay those expenses.
Funds for long-term care can come from a traditional policy for such care, a hybrid policy that allows you to withdraw cash to cover such expenses, or from your own assets – if you have it.
Prepare legal documents: This will prevent court battles.
Designate a trusted healthcare attorney who will supervise it and make sure that the right people follow your will if communication becomes impossible.
Also consider hiring an attorney to handle your finances.
Choose a trusted person, because she will make financial decisions for you and make sure that all bills are paid if you are unable to do it yourself.
Don’t forget the details: Imagine that your elderly parent suddenly needs medical attention and is going to the hospital right now.
Can you answer questions about medications and allergies?
Write out all the information in order to have it prepared.
“It’s not just about finances, it’s about who the doctors are,” Martin asks.
“What medications do you take?
Who will take care of the dog?
It’s important to have such a plan at hand.”
A man repeatedly shot from a windbreaker in Ilfracombe
The man was repeatedly shot from a windbreaker as he returned home from an evening party.
The forty-something-year-old was in the Oxford Grové area of Ilfracombe in Devon County when he was shot in the chest, abdomen and hand.
Police officers described the shooting, which took place at about 02:30 BST time, as an "accidental action."
Victim couldn't see the attacker.
The injuries sustained are not threatening the life of the man. The police are asking for witnesses to the incident to come forward.
Earthquakes and tsunamis in Indonesia
According to official reports, at least 384 people died as a result of the massive earthquake and tsunami that struck the Indonesian city of Palu on Friday. The number of casualties will probably increase.
Due to broken communication, the rescuers were unable to obtain any information from Donggala's cabupaten, which is located to the north of Palu, closer to the epicenter of the 7.5-degree earthquake.
More than 16 000 people were evacuated after the Palu disaster.
Here are some of the most important informations about the city of Palu and Cabupaten Donggala on Celebes Island:
Palu is the capital of Celebes Central, a province located at the end of a narrow bay on the western coast of the island. According to estimates, in 2017 it was inhabited by 379 800 people.
When there was an earthquake and tsunami, the 40th anniversary of its founding was celebrated in the city.
Donggala is a cabupaten (an administrative unit lower from the province) stretching along the north-west coast of the island for more than 300 km.
It is estimated that in 2017 it was inhabited by 299 200 people.
The main branches of the economy of Celebes of Central are fisheries and agriculture, which have developed especially in Donggal's cabupaten on the coast.
Another source of income for the province are nickel mines, but they are located mainly in Morowali, on the opposite coast of Celebes.
According to the Indonesian Disastroct Elimination Agency over the past 100 years, earthquakes and tsunamis have haunted Palu and Donggala several times.
In 1938, a tsunami that hit Donggala killed more than 200 people and destroyed hundreds of homes.
In 1996, nine people were killed in a tsunami in West Donggali.
Indonesia is located on a seismically active Pacific rinl of fire, so earthquakes occur there quite regularly.
The largest earthquakes and tsunamis in recent years:
2004: A major quake on December 26 hit the west coast of Aceh province in the north of Sumatra triggered a tsunami that hit 14 countries, killing 226,000 people on the Indian Ocean coast, more than half in Aceh.
2005: At the end of March and the beginning of April, Sumatra's west coast was visited by a series of strong earthquakes.
Hundreds of people have been killed on the island of Nias off the coast of Sumatra.
2006: In southern Java, Indonesia's most populous island, there was a 6.8-degree quake, triggering a tsunami that stormed into the southern coast, killing nearly 700 people.
2099: A 7.6-degree quake took place near Padang, the capital of Western Sumatra.
More than 1,100 people were killed.
2010: A magnitude 7.5 earthquake struck one of the Mentawai islands near the coast of Sumatra. It triggered a tsunami wave up to 10 meters high, which destroyed dozens of villages and killed about 300 people.
2016) The shallow quake hit Pidie Jay's cabupaten in Aceh province, causing destruction and panic among the people who still remembered the damage that the devastating 2004 earthquake and tsunami brought.
This time there was no tsunami, but collapsing buildings killed more than 100 people.
2018: Big Earthquakes hit Indonesia's tourist island, Lombok, killing more than 500 people, mostly on its northern side.
They destroyed thousands of homes and caused temporary trouble for thousands of tourists.
Sara Palin's eldest son arrested for domestic violence
