The analyst reconstructed the events of the night the woman was burned alive
On Saturday, the prosecutor's office completed presenting evidence in the re-trial of a man accused of burning a woman alive in Mississippi in 2014.
An analyst from the U.S. Department of Judiciary, Paul Rowlett, testified for hours as a forensic expert on information analysis.
